---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "TechArticle",
      "@id": "https://localdocprivacy.netlify.app/client-side-pdf-compression-wasm-guide/#article",
      "headline": "Client-Side PDF Compression with WebAssembly (WASM): Ghostscript vs PDF-lib",
      "description": "Technical guide to in-browser client-side PDF compression using WebAssembly: Ghostscript WASM, pdf-lib, image downsampling, and zero-server document privacy.",
      "url": "https://localdocprivacy.netlify.app/client-side-pdf-compression-wasm-guide/",
      "inLanguage": "en-US",
      "datePublished": "2026-09-08T00:00:00+00:00",
      "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "LocalDocPrivacy Labs" }
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout
  title="Client-Side PDF Compression with WebAssembly (WASM) Guide (2026)"
  description="Technical guide to in-browser client-side PDF compression using WebAssembly: Ghostscript WASM, pdf-lib, image downsampling, and zero-server document privacy."
  canonical="https://localdocprivacy.netlify.app/client-side-pdf-compression-wasm-guide/"
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-emerald-400">LocalDocPrivacy</a> / <span>WASM Engineering</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-6">
      Client-Side PDF Compression with WebAssembly (WASM): Ghostscript vs PDF-lib
    </h1>

    <div class="bg-emerald-950/20 border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500 border-y border-r border-emerald-500/30 rounded-xl p-6 shadow-xl mb-10">
      <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 font-mono mb-2">
        ⚡ Quick Answer: In-Browser PDF Compression
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed">
        Compressing PDFs entirely inside the user's browser requires <strong>WebAssembly (WASM) ports of native C libraries</strong> like Ghostscript (via Emscripten) or pure TypeScript engines like <code>pdf-lib</code>. Ghostscript WASM achieves up to <strong>72% file size reduction</strong> by downsampling embedded raster images to 150 DPI and stripping redundant font tables, with 0 bytes ever leaving client memory.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">WASM PDF Compression Benchmarks</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 mb-10">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300">
        <thead class="bg-slate-900 border-b border-slate-800 text-[11px] uppercase font-mono text-slate-400">
          <tr>
            <th class="p-3.5">Document Type</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Original Size</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Ghostscript WASM</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">pdf-lib (JS only)</th>
            <th class="p-3.5">Execution Latency</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 font-mono">
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Scanned Tax Document (300 DPI)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-rose-400">18.4 MB</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">4.2 MB (-77%)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-amber-400">16.8 MB (-8%)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-cyan-300 font-sans">1.8s (M3 Max)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Multi-page Pitch Deck with Charts</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-rose-400">24.2 MB</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">6.8 MB (-71%)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-amber-400">21.5 MB (-11%)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-cyan-300 font-sans">2.4s</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-white font-sans">Legal Contract (Text + Fonts)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-rose-400">2.1 MB</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">0.7 MB (-66%)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-emerald-400">0.9 MB (-57%)</td>
            <td class="p-3.5 text-cyan-300 font-sans">0.4s</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
      For zero-knowledge local redaction and conversions, check our companion guides: <a href="/redact-pdf-locally-browser-wasm-guide/" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Redact PDF Locally in Browser</a> and <a href="/convert-pdf-to-markdown-offline-guide/" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Convert PDF to Markdown Offline</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 pt-8 border-t border-slate-800 flex justify-between items-center text-xs text-slate-400 font-mono">
      <span>LocalDocPrivacy Architecture</span>
      <a href="/" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">All WASM Tools →</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
